{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"78be9a694e89b8fd53f9cc710705f9b9c3feafb6e8acac0035676ec97a194f70","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review gate / plan-review block decision","key_entities":["code_review_result_v1","pass3_decide/decide.py","block_threshold","priority","validity","impact","docs/experiments/derive_code_review_threshold.py","code_review_adjudication.jsonl","tests/unit/test_derive_code_review_threshold.py"],"problem_keywords":["code-review gate","blocking threshold","impact model calibration","precision-crossover","false positives","finding adjudication"],"propositions":["The code-review gate has cast zero BLOCK votes across 162 changes despite 76% carrying advisories and confirmed must-fix findings, indicating the 0.95 default threshold is unreachable given the observed impact distribution ceiling at 0.60.","The block decision thresholds on priority (validity × impact), not raw impact, so the derived threshold must be computed as the smallest priority value t where precision(block-worthy | priority >= t) exceeds 0.5.","The adjudicated corpus must project stored validity/impact/priority fields from code_review_result_v1 sidecars (blocking/advisory buckets) and classify each finding as block-worthy, not-block-worthy, or ambiguous based on post-merge evidence (follow-up fixes, red-main incidents).","The 0.54 priority band (including #518 security finding) and whether the 0.60 ceiling captures only max-priority findings must be explicitly analyzed to justify the final threshold selection.","The derivation logic must be unit-tested under tests/ and the chosen threshold committed as a verifiable repo artifact under docs/experiments/ before the block enablement can proceed."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785822246262596318,"uuid":"b24a00ee-50e6-49fd-9579-adf7166f4aaf"}